{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they said.</b> This name, the God of the Hebrews — for they were known, and this is Abraham, who was called a Hebrew, and Isaac his son, and Jacob and his sons, as I shall explain regarding the verse \"when you acquire a Hebrew slave\" (below 21:2)." "<b>And they said.</b> The word נקרה is like נקרא נקריתי בהר הגלבוע (II Samuel 1:6), and it has the sense of encountering. And behold, he explained to him why they are obligated to hold a festival, lest a plague or sword come." "The word פן יפגענו includes us Israelites, also you Pharaoh with us and all the Egyptians. And when Pharaoh saw that the wild beasts came and devoured many Egyptians, as it is written ישלח בהם ערוב ויאכלם (Psalms 78:45), then he said לכו זבחו לאלהיכם בארץ (below 5:21). And Moses answered him: it is not proper to do so in the land; rather, a journey of three days into the wilderness — they shall go far. And this distance is between Egypt and Mount Sinai for one walking a straight path, and there they sacrificed, as written תעבדון את האלהים על ההר הזה (above 3:12), and also ויבן משה מזבח תחת ההר (below 24:4). Also the altar he built at the battle with Amalek is at Mount Sinai, for it is written ויחנו ברפידים (below 17:1), and there it is written הנני עומד לפניך שם על הצור בחורב (ibid. ibid. 6). And at the plague of locusts he gave permission to some of Israel to go and sacrifice, and at the plague of darkness he gave permission for all to go — only their livestock would not go with them. And when they saw that the plague came and struck the firstborn, then the words of Moses were confirmed to them — פן יפגענו בדבר — therefore they said כולנו מתים (below 12:33). And the Egyptians drove them out to go and sacrifice, and also lent to them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {2 "Comment [2] in the original has no bold lemma head; it continues directly from comment [1]'s discussion of פן יפגענו. Translated as presented."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:56.198429331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}